# Parcel Optimization

Tooling for a UPS/FedEx parcel rate negotiation and gain-share business — analyzing carrier agreements and invoices to find negotiation opportunities, then verifying and invoicing on realized savings.

## Status

Early-stage. Repo created ahead of any code — structure and scope are still being defined.

## Background

Small and mid-size shippers ($200k–$2M in annual parcel spend) are typically underserved by enterprise-focused parcel audit platforms and too complex to self-serve on free tools. This project explores automating the recurring, mechanical parts of that engagement — lead research, savings verification, and invoicing — while keeping the negotiation itself expertise-driven.

## Planned Components

- **Lead research** — identify and enrich candidate shippers in the target spend band
- **Baseline capture** — structured representation of a client's existing carrier agreement (discounts, accessorials, minimums, tier thresholds)
- **Savings verification** — reprice weekly carrier invoices against the baseline to calculate realized savings
- **Invoicing** — generate gain-share invoices with line-item backup

## Stack (tentative)

- n8n for scheduled/recurring workflows
- Google Sheets/Airtable for interim data storage
- Claude for judgment-heavy research and analysis steps

## Notes

Scope and architecture are not final. This README will be updated as the project takes shape.
